---
/*
 * What only a title-as-index sidebar needs: the disclosure upgrade for its chevrons,
 * and the layout that puts a chevron on its label's row (ADR-0075).
 *
 * `CustomSidebarBody` renders this outside `<sl-sidebar-state-persist>`: a script in
 * there would break the parity test, and could hit the Safari/VoiceOver bug
 * `SidebarPersister.astro` documents for a `display: contents` container.
 *
 * ## The layout
 * `summary` has to stay in `details`, and the upgrade's button sits just before it, so
 * neither can share a row with the label in normal flow. Both are placed on that row
 * from the `li` instead, in the same box (NFR-006), and the label stops short of it, so
 * the current page's highlight never runs under a chevron. A closed `details` then has
 * no height, and an open one has only its list.
 *
 * ## Why not scoped, and why not layered
 * The button a script creates has no scope attribute. `disclosure.css` is unlayered, so
 * a rule in `starlight.core` would lose to it; the doubled class wins over it whatever
 * the order the sheets load in. `display` is not set here, so its
 * `.dk-disclosure--upgraded > details > summary { display: none }` still applies.
 */
---

<script>
	import '../../lib/disclosure/disclosure.client.js';
</script>

<style is:global>
	.dk-group {
		position: relative;
	}

	.dk-group.dk-disclosure > .dk-group__label {
		margin-inline-end: 2.25rem;
	}

	.dk-group.dk-disclosure > details > summary,
	.dk-group.dk-disclosure > .dk-disclosure__toggle {
		position: absolute;
		inset-block-start: 0;
		inset-inline-end: 0;
		inline-size: 2.25rem; /* centres a 1.25rem caret where a plain group's sits */
		block-size: 2.25rem; /* the label row on a phone */
		justify-content: center;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50rem) {
		.dk-group.dk-disclosure > details > summary,
		.dk-group.dk-disclosure > .dk-disclosure__toggle {
			block-size: 2rem; /* the label row from 50rem up */
		}
	}

	.dk-group.dk-disclosure > details > summary > svg,
	.dk-group.dk-disclosure > .dk-disclosure__toggle > svg {
		inline-size: 1.25rem;
		block-size: 1.25rem;
	}
</style>
